    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nObligatory thanks for the awesome module and for your time and contributions :)\n\nI thought it might be intuitive if the default `gx` keymap, mapped to `vim.ui.open` worked seamlessly in the file explorer. I don't know if this is the sort of thing you want to add to mini.nvim directly, mention in the docs, or just not worry about at all. Since no one has requested this before (at least according to my github issue-searching skills), I don't think this is super important :D.\n\nHere is the keymap I've been using\n\n```\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gx\", function() vim.ui.open(minifiles.get_fs_entry().path) end, {\n  buffer = buf_id,\n  desc = \"vim.ui.open\",\n})\n```",
