            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion and kind words!\n\nThis should be resolved on latest `main`.\n\nI initially didn't really understand the use case, but it indeed might be useful for non-text files (and maybe sometimes directories). As 'mini.files' is mostly about dealing with text files, I don't really want to add it as built-in. Besides, its obvious left-hand-side `gx` will conflict with 'exchange' operator from 'mini.operators' (more details in e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64 commit message). So I decided to add it as example, as it is pretty concise and is a good way to deal with non-text files from 'mini.files' (if one wants to).",
